 ## How the kanji combine
 
-This is the noun associated with [締め切る](締め切る.md) (しめきる), "close up; close applications." 締め contributes closing, and [切](../kanji/切.md) contributes completing the action, not cutting a submitted paper.
+This is the noun associated with [締め切る](締め切る.md) (しめきる), "close up; close applications." [締](../kanji/締.md)め contributes closing, and [切](../kanji/切.md) contributes completing the action, not cutting a submitted paper.
 
 The separate physical sense is closing a door or window, also written 閉め切り with [閉](../kanji/閉.md). The list's "Closed/No Entrance" glosses need a notice context: a closed opening can explain an entry notice, while application acceptance can also be closed at a deadline. They do not make 締め切り a general expression for every prohibition on entry.
 
